{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/contract/clax-extensions.d.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:04:13.717971Z","id":"dbb3f8a4af960c891c35f4acbff42152dafadbc6ce81d1822beda2f284a3d1df","body":{"detail":"After DELETE /api/artifacts/<A>/db-grants/<B>, the hub (crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs reader_routes, the per-event may_read check) stops sending B's doc events on docs:<B>?reader=<A>, so web/shell/src/caps/cross-read.ts onStream (line 164) never schedules a refetch and the error callback is not called. web/e2e/db-artifact.spec.ts:84-85 pins exactly that: after the revoke, #runs keeps '5,7' and #err stays ''. The subscription, its stream topic and the page's last snapshot stay until a ready/resync triggers a refused refetch. The same text is in apps/clax_app/assets/prompt/clax-extensions.d.ts:80-85, which the app's agent reads, and cross-read.ts:19-20 and record 44415b80 describe the ending as if it followed the revoke. Live updates do stop at once, so no new data of B reaches the page.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:a8c8dc35","span":{"start":{"line":80},"end":{"line":85},"content_hash":"e3646f1e969299c351c53532bf2a7050fd9e5d6f6c7c535ed580c25c5aa9f635"},"suggested_fix":"Either state the behaviour (a revoke stops further snapshots; the error callback runs when the view next reconnects) in both .d.ts copies, or have the shell learn of the revoke (for instance the daemon sending refused on the reader topic when a grant is deleted) and end the listener then.","summary":"The contract says a revoked grant ends a live db.artifact(id) listener with not_granted, but the listener only stops receiving: it ends at the stream's next ready or resync","tags":["review","W3","contract","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/contract/clax-extensions.d.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:07:32.893293Z","id":"1dc0eff151c99c00b7fa52e00d09f58b62cb3386f1e617e607ef594611004f1c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:215522bf","summary":"The DbCrossReadErrorCode doc now says a revoke stops live updates at once and the listener hears not_granted at its next refresh (a stream reconnect), and later get() rejects not_granted; apps/clax_app/assets/prompt/clax-extensions.d.ts synced (scripts/sync-app-prompt.sh --check passes)","supersedes":"dbb3f8a4af960c891c35f4acbff42152dafadbc6ce81d1822beda2f284a3d1df","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
